/* The runtime's entry points the host calls, the class-library table's
 * slots by name and its slot count, the exported name installed in each
 * filled slot, and the managed-side declarations the runtime's own
 * bootstrapper carries, at tag v11.0.0-rc.2.26504.105 (commit 820230c386db5b0106c5430b3e5aee92a7826bf5).
 * GENERATED by the runtime entry-point reader from startup.cpp (sha256
 * bf41dd8c027dae516091659640bec888e9e6618ee43182a860915729e557cccf), unix/UnixNativeCodeManager.cpp (sha256
 * 7f35e4917386e584e7467bb2ff8ecd60c62ba47863b1f7f88f5684cdb01cdfad), ICodeManager.h (sha256
 * 1fecdd995987646d4407d24e228fbaaec6b09a5ae1cabd4d141ea464d9e3e970) and Bootstrap/main.cpp (sha256
 * 7b15cc4ecaa6ddb7f432f87c57c8d6f3fe0b7da97fa36c6e9bd9b8f51bc2b6a9): the prototypes are the definitions' own,
 * never typed in by hand; regenerate at a re-pin, never edit by hand. The
 * table is indexed by the runtime's own enum, dense from zero, and each
 * slot below carries the index that enum gives it; the ranges the
 * registration takes are a start address and a length in bytes. The
 * exported names are the bootstrapper's own table entries in slot order,
 * each checked to end in its slot's enum name; the slots of the build
 * feature the Unix build lacks are null and carry no name. */
